ourt N","lastName":"Bittencourt","firstName":"Najara","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"de Melo Silva NG","lastName":"de Melo Silva","firstName":"Natália Guedes","initials":"NG"},{"fullName":"de Oliveira Saraiva P","lastName":"de Oliveira Saraiva","firstName":"Priscilla","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"de Sousa Monteiro Q","lastName":"de Sousa Monteiro","firstName":"Quézia","initials":"Q"},{"fullName":"Dos Santos RT","lastName":"Dos Santos","firstName":"Rafael Theodoro","initials":"RT"},{"fullName":"Freire RS","lastName":"Freire","firstName":"Raíssa Soares","initials":"RS"},{"fullName":"de Araújo Pinto RA","lastName":"de Araújo Pinto","firstName":"Rebecca Augusta","initials":"RA"},{"fullName":"Ferreira RB","lastName":"Ferreira","firstName":"Reinan Brotas","initials":"RB"},{"fullName":"de Lima RS","lastName":"de Lima","firstName":"Rodrigo Saboia","initials":"RS"},{"fullName":"de Melo RFT","lastName":"de Melo","firstName":"Rosângela Francisca Tanantas","initials":"RFT"},{"fullName":"Saenz ST","lastName":"Saenz","firstName":"Sabrina Teixeira","initials":"ST"},{"fullName":"Alvarez Fernandes SS","lastName":"Alvarez Fernandes","firstName":"Salete Sara","initials":"SS"},{"fullName":"Vítor-Silva S","lastName":"Vítor-Silva","firstName":"Sheila","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"de Oliveira TMR","lastName":"de Oliveira","firstName":"Tânia Maria Rodrigues","initials":"TMR"},{"fullName":"Tavella TA","lastName":"Tavella","firstName":"Tatyana A","initials":"TA"},{"fullName":"Câmara TT","lastName":"Câmara","firstName":"Thais Tavares","initials":"TT"},{"fullName":"Santos TC","lastName":"Santos","firstName":"Thalie Cavalcante","initials":"TC"},{"fullName":"Pinto TS","lastName":"Pinto","firstName":"Thiago Serrão","initials":"TS"},{"fullName":"Dos Santos TWR","lastName":"Dos Santos","firstName":"Tilza Waleska Rocha","initials":"TWR"},{"fullName":"do Nascimento VA","lastName":"do Nascimento","firstName":"Valdinete Alves","initials":"VA"},{"fullName":"Sousa Barbosa WP","lastName":"Sousa Barbosa","firstName":"Wanessa Pessoa","initials":"WP"},{"fullName":"de Melo WF","lastName":"de Melo","firstName":"Wellinthon Ferreira","initials":"WF"},{"fullName":"Salgado Sobrinho WB","lastName":"Salgado Sobrinho","firstName":"Wlademir Braga","initials":"WB"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5645-2055"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6702-5681"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8486-7469"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9134-3970"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9755-9668"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9995-0249"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0848-1940"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1495-2489"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2888-1060"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6127-0544"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6458-0900"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9836-7868"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0875-7596"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1102-2419"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1425-926X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1659-3763"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-3374-9985"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-2566-4107"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"9","volume":"72","journalIssueId":3164740,"dateOfPublication":"2021 May","monthOfPublication":5,"yearOfPublication":2021,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Clin Infect Dis","title":"Clinical infectious diseases : an official publication of the Infectious Diseases Society of America","essn":"1537-6591","issn":"1058-4838","nlmid":"9203213","isoabbreviation":"Clin Infect Dis"},"printPublicationDate":"2021-05-01"},"pubYear":"2021","pageInfo":"e373-e381","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Steroid use for coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) is based on the possible role of these drugs in mitigating the inflammatory response, mainly in the lungs, triggered by severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2). This study aimed to evaluate the efficacy of methylprednisolone (MP) among hospitalized patients with suspected COVID-19.<h4>Methods</h4>A parallel, double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized, Phase IIb clinical trial was performed with hospitalized patients aged ≥18 years with clinical, epidemiological, and/or radiological suspected COVID-19 at a tertiary care facility in Manaus, Brazil. Patients were randomly allocated (1:1 ratio) to receive either intravenous MP (0.5 mg/kg) or placebo (saline solution) twice daily for 5 days. A modified intention-to-treat (mITT) analysis was conducted. The primary outcome was 28-day mortality.<h4>Results</h4>From 18 April to 16 June 2020, 647 patients were screened, 416 were randomized, and 393 were analyzed as mITT, with 194 individuals assigned to MP and 199 to placebo. SARS-CoV-2 infection was confirmed by reverse transcriptase polymerase chain reaction in 81.3%. The mortality rates at Day 28 were not different between groups. A subgroup analysis showed that patients over 60 years old in the MP group had a lower mortality rate at Day 28. Patients in the MP arm tended to need more insulin therapy, and no difference was seen in virus clearance in respiratory secretion until Day 7.<h4>Conclusions</h4>The findings of this study suggest that a short course of MP in hospitalized patients with COVID-19 did not reduce mortality in the overall population.<h4>Clinical trials registration</h4>NCT04343729.","affiliation":"Fundação de Medicina Tropical Dr. Heitor Vieira Dourado, Manaus, Brazil.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado do Amazonas","grantId":"PAPAC 005/2019","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico","grantId":"403253/2020-9","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","gra